# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Gemini. This is the only AI provider SafeShift uses: it drives the
# agent under test, the red-team attacker, and the judge.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Server-side only — it is read by the Gemini client used from API routes,
# the CLI, MCP server, SDK, and scripts; it never reaches the browser bundle.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the Gemini model used for every AI role. Leave unset to use the
# application's current default. One crash test can make multiple API requests,
# so choose a model and quota appropriate for your environment.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Maya Research TTS — powers the spoken read-back in the voice scenario
# composer and the "hear the call" playback. Voice is optional; everything
# else works without it. https://docs.mayaresearch.ai
# MAYA_API_KEY=
